  "descriptionMarkdown": "# Introduction\n\nA compact factory for Fulgora. It produces all intermediate products. It also builds rockets to send them to space platforms. No quality items required. No Tier 3 modules needed.\n\nThis is my early-game solution for Fulgora. Land on the planet. Build this factory and a large accumulator array. Then I can leave Fulgora alone until endgame.\n\n# V2 Update:\n\n1. Reduced footprint to 53×20 (previously 68×26). Including the Output Nullifier (recycling system for handling outputs), total dimensions are 58×42.\n2. Decreased power consumption to approximately 120MW (down from 220MW).\n3. Relocated provider chest closer to rocket silo for more efficient item transfer.\n4. Under optimal conditions (scrap recycling productivity level ≥ 9 and no non-science items requested), SPM can reach 90.\n# V1 Description:\n\nA compact (68x26 size) Fulgora outpost that makes science packs and three Fulgora-specific items.\n\nInitially, it achieves about 55 SPM; with scrap recycling productivity 6 or 7, it reaches about 85 SPM.\n\nThis setup uses maximum productivity module 2 to process holmium ore. If you want to save scrap, use circuit conditions to cut off the input if enough science packs and Fulgora-specific items have been cached in passive provider chests. It is not very easy to write a reliable rule to keep enough of four different items but not waste scrap, though.\n\n### Input\n1. Two red belts of scrap\n2. Heavy oil (from the ocean)\n3. 220 MW power\n\n### Output\n1. Two red belts of unused scrap, must be used or destroyed quickly (see picture).\n\n### Upgrade\nAfter Vulcanus, you can replace the two assembly machine 3s for holmium plate with one foundry with full productivity modules to boost the production of items other than science packs. (The picture has already been upgraded with foundry.)\n\nAfter Gleba, you can set up some heating towers at its output, using ice and solid fuel for power generation.",
